---
title: Roast Potatoes
description: Traditional accompaniment to a roast dinner
course: Side
locale: en_GB
prep time: 20m
cook time: 55m
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: British
tags:
- side-dish
- savoury
- british
---

Preheat oven to 180°C.

Place the @Maris Piper or Kind Edward potatoes{1%kg}(peeled and chopped) in a saucepan and barely cover with water. Bring to the boil and then simmer reasonably vigorously for ~{2%minutes}.

Heat the @duck or goose fat{100%g}(or olive oil) in a roasting tin large enough to spread the potatoes into a single layer.

Drain the potatoes in a colander and shake to fluff up the outsides. Sprinkle with the @flour{2%tsp} and shake until evenly and thinly coated.

Carefully put the potatoes in the hot fat. Turn until coated all over, and spread into a single layer.

Roast for ~{15%minutes}, then turn the potatoes over.

Roast for a further ~{15%minutes}, then turn the potatoes over again.

Roast for a final 10 to ~{20%minutes} until golden and crisp.